\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A quick way to rename with or with sequential numbers, simple\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Continuous capture buffer for the ADFX recorder strip.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 REAPER only writes a recording while the transport is rolling, which is no use for an instrument that is played live against a stopped project. A JSFX has no such limit: @sample runs whenever audio is flowing through the track, transport or not. So this plug-in keeps the last few minutes of whatever reaches it in a ring buffer, and hands a slice of that buffer to the project on request. Nothing here touches the transport.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 It is loaded, configured and driven by ADFX_Recorder_Buffer.lua. There is nothing to set by hand.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
